# The Boeing 737-300: JSBSim's 737 made to fly to its airport-planning document's
# and type certificate's figures (assets/figures/737-300.xml) by tools/make_737_300.py.
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name Boeing 737-300
model 737-300
class airliner
start 250 0.53
# The speedbrake lever works its speedbrakes or spoilers (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).
speedbrakes
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# Boeing D6-58325-6 rev E, 7.2.4: H40x14.5-19 mains at 201 psi loaded,
# at 140,000 lb. Her Hydro-Aire Hytrol Mark III anti-skid is taken as fully
# modulating: the FAA's braking working group (2019) puts its efficiency
# within 5 per cent of a digital system's; no document names its class.
brakes 201 fully-modulating
# Her CFM56-3s' cascade thrust reversers (tools/make_737_300.py), and the
# reverse brought to idle at 60 kt: Boeing's 737 Flight Crew Training Manual
# (as excerpted in NTSB DCA19MA143, attachment 17) - "Reverse thrust is
# reduced to idle between 60 KIAS and taxi speed" (docs/ASSETS.md).
reversers 60
